    {
      "id": 224559,
      "name": "Rabit",
      "username": "Rabit",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
      "created_at": "2018-12-06T00:11:59.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Some things that came up in our experiences/discussions from PAX Unplugged. Spoilers, so don’t read unless you are planning to GM (or aren’t planning to play and are curious).&nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>[color=white]If you want to hold to the intended flavor of the initial encounter, add to Myriad's HP as noted. If you want to have a more positive encounter, don't. It's still a challending encounter, but it's far more enjoyable of an experience for the players. [/color]</li>\n\t<li>[color=white]There are... different opinions on how to handle Myriad's \"Release the Swarm\" ability. :-\\ For example, some folks interpret the \"of Min die size\" to mean a die size of around the result of the Min die. So a \"3\" on the Min die would give d4 minions. Others interpretted it to mean of the size of the Min die -- which is a very different (and deadlier!) result. Since he's probably using Insect Control (d10), Swarm Master (d8), and will have 0 minions (d12), the [b][i]smallest[/i][/b] die it could be is a d8 minion! :-o And it was not uncommon to have the Max die be 10-12, so that's a huge number of large minions. (FYI: Christopher said he interpretted it to be the latter.)[/color]</li>\n</ul>",
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:57:58.779Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
